diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 5680409..4726661 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 - `slotwise.reminders.reminder_text(appointment)` builds the SMS reminder: plain ASCII (umlauts as ae/oe/ue), the reception number 044 512 77 30, and at most 160 characters. Cancelled appointments are refused.
 - `Schedule.book_series(therapist, client, start, treatment, sessions)` books weekly sessions at the same weekday and time. A week whose slot is taken is skipped and a later week is used instead. Series of more than 9 sessions are refused, and a series is either fully booked or not booked at all.
 - `Schedule.week(therapist, monday)` returns a therapist's non-cancelled appointments for the seven days from `monday`, as a dict from date to a list sorted by start time. Days with no appointments map to an empty list.
+- `Schedule.reschedule(appointment_id, new_start)` moves an appointment to a new start time, keeping its treatment and therapist. It runs the same opening-hours and changeover checks as booking, ignoring the appointment's own current slot, and changes nothing if refused. Cancelled appointments cannot be moved.
 - `Schedule.cancel(appointment_id)` marks an appointment as cancelled (`status` field) instead of deleting it. Cancelled appointments no longer block their slot or changeover gap, and the status is saved to JSON.
 
